6. NOT A MEDICAL DEVICE

OCRadar is an awareness tool. It is not a medical device, and it does not
provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. It has not been reviewed,
evaluated, or cleared by the FDA or any other regulatory body.

It does not screen for, detect, diagnose, assess, or rule out any condition,
including cancer. It compares an image against reference categories and
reports which of them look similar. That comparison can be wrong in both
directions. Only a dentist or physician can examine a lesion.

Nothing in this repository — the app, the ML pipeline, any trained model, or
any output of either — may be deployed, distributed, described, or otherwise
represented as a screening or diagnostic tool. See MedicalDisclaimer in
OCRadarKit/Sources/OCRCore for the canonical user-facing wording, which is
the only wording the product uses.
